tokio 1.53.2: build the NetBSD peer-credential code for NetBSD only

src/net/unix/ucred.rs compiles impl_netbsd for target_os = "nto" as well,
although QNX uses impl_nto (getpeereid()). impl_netbsd imports
libc::LOCAL_PEEREID, which libc defines for the QNX 7.x io-pkt stack only
(target_env nto70/nto71); QNX 8 (io-sock) has no LOCAL_PEEREID in its
headers and gives peer credentials through getpeereid() in <unistd.h>. So
for nto80 the crate stopped with
error[E0432]: unresolved import `libc::LOCAL_PEEREID`.
Restrict the module to NetBSD, as tokio 1.54.1 does.

Upstream-Status: Backport [tokio 1.54.1, src/net/unix/ucred.rs]
---
--- a/src/net/unix/ucred.rs
+++ b/src/net/unix/ucred.rs
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
     }
 }
 
-#[cfg(any(target_os = "netbsd", target_os = "nto"))]
+#[cfg(target_os = "netbsd")]
 pub(crate) mod impl_netbsd {
     use crate::net::unix::{self, UnixStream};
 
